# For Terrain Cache (the hooks' TerrainCache.cs). The terrain's prepare pass clears the mesh's vertex colours, its
# modifiers add theirs premultiplied, and the finalize pass turns them into straight colours where they are: run again
# without the passes before it, it would divide them by their alpha once more each frame (the Moon's ground goes white).
# The hooks build this shader a second time with PORT_TERRAIN_CACHE_HIT defined and bind that build when they skip the
# prepare and modifier passes: the colours of the frame slot's last full run, which had the same inputs, stay as they
# are. Without the define the shader is the game's.

@@ edit terrain-cache-colors Planet/TerrainMesh/FinalizeModifiers.comp
@@ what kept the terrain's colours as they are when the terrain cache reuses them
@@ find
    outColors[gl_GlobalInvocationID.x] = PremultipliedAlphaToStraight(outColors[gl_GlobalInvocationID.x]);
@@ replace
#ifndef PORT_TERRAIN_CACHE_HIT  // macOS port: Terrain Cache's build keeps the straight colours already there
    outColors[gl_GlobalInvocationID.x] = PremultipliedAlphaToStraight(outColors[gl_GlobalInvocationID.x]);
#endif
